cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "tss-sim: modelling and simulation for a low-SWaP FMCW topside ionospheric sounder"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Moss
    given-names: Andrew B.
    affiliation: "Utah State University, Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end simulator for a frequency modulated continuous wave topside
  ionospheric sounder small enough to fly on a nanosatellite.  The package is
  layered truth-in and profile-out, from an ionosphere state model through
  propagation, instrument, signal processing and retrieval to an assessment
  scored against a traced requirement set.  It carries a corrected sensitivity
  model for spaceborne HF sounding, a derived and archive-validated lower edge
  for the sounding band, and the algorithms for separating Doppler shift from
  range using spacecraft motion alone.
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
keywords:
  - ionosphere
  - topside sounder
  - FMCW radar
  - CubeSat
  - high frequency
